From: rx550-g5
Subject: [PATCH] backends/drm: pick the legacy ADDFB depth from the buffer format

When ADDFB2 returns EOPNOTSUPP (big-endian kernels without
quirk_addfb_prefer_host_byte_order, e.g. amdgpu on PowerPC), KWin fell back to
drmModeAddFB(depth 24, bpp 32) for every buffer. 10-bit (AR30/AB30) scanout buffers were then
shown as XRGB8888 (garbled colours) and the ARGB cursor lost its alpha. Map XRGB8888/ARGB8888/
XRGB2101010 to their legacy depths and fail for formats ADDFB cannot express, so the format
selection moves on to a usable one.

--- ka/src/backends/drm/drm_gpu.cpp
+++ kb/src/backends/drm/drm_gpu.cpp
@@ -1003,11 +1003,28 @@
                             attributes->offset.data(),
                             &framebufferId,
                             0);
-        if (ret == -EOPNOTSUPP && attributes->planeCount == 1) {
+        // Legacy ADDFB can only express a few formats through depth/bpp. Big-endian kernels
+        // without ADDFB2 get here for every buffer, so never label 10-bit or alpha buffers as
+        // XRGB8888 (that showed garbled colours and a cursor without alpha).
+        int legacyDepth = 0;
+        switch (attributes->format) {
+        case DRM_FORMAT_XRGB8888:
+            legacyDepth = 24;
+            break;
+        case DRM_FORMAT_ARGB8888:
+            legacyDepth = 32;
+            break;
+        case DRM_FORMAT_XRGB2101010:
+            legacyDepth = 30;
+            break;
+        default:
+            break;
+        }
+        if (ret == -EOPNOTSUPP && attributes->planeCount == 1 && legacyDepth != 0) {
             ret = drmModeAddFB(m_fd,
                                attributes->width,
                                attributes->height,
-                               24, 32,
+                               legacyDepth, 32,
                                attributes->pitch[0],
                                handles[0],
                                &framebufferId);
